hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"387","'Abdullah said, Lying is not correct"","" neither  in seriousness nor in jest. None of you should promise his child something and then not give it to him."""
"388","Ibn 'Umar reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, The believer who mixes with people and endures their injury is better than the person who does not mix with people nor endure their injury."""
"389","Abu Musa reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, No one - nothing - is more patient in enduring an injury which he hears than Allah Almighty. They claim that He has a son"","" and yet He still cures them and provides for them."""
"390","Umar bin Hafs narrated to us, saying: Abu narrated to us, saying: Al-A'mash narrated to us, saying: I heard Shaqiq saying: Abdullah said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) distributed the spoils, as He distributes, and a man from the Ansar said: By Allah, it is a distribution as I intended, in accordance with the Face of Allah, the Exalted, the Glorious. I said: I will say it to the Prophet (peace be upon him), so I went to him, and he was among his companions, so I approached him, and he turned his face away from me, and his countenance changed, and he was angry, until I wished I had not informed him. Then he said: Moses was afflicted with more than this, and he was patient."","" may Allah bless him and grant him peace"","" swore an oath like one of the oaths that people swear and a man of the Ansar said"","" 'By Allah"","" it is not an oath by which the Face of Allah Almighty is desired."" I said"","" 'I will tell the Prophet"","" may Allah bless him and grant him peace. I went to him while he was with his Companions and I spoke to him in confidence. It clearly affected him greatly"","" may Allah bless him and grant him peace"","" and his face changed colour so that I wished that I had not told him. Then he said"","" 'Musa was injured with greater than that and he endured it.'"""
"391","Abu'd-Darda' reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, Shall I tell you a degree better than prayer"","" fasting and sadaqa?"" ""Yes"","" they replied. He went to say"","" Improving a state of friendship. Causing discord in a state of friendship is what shaves things away."""
"392","Fear Allah and put things right between you"","" (8:1)"","" Ibn 'Abbas said"","" ""This is an injunction from Allah to the believers to fear Allah and to put things right between them."""
"393","Sufyan ibn Usayd al-Hadrami reported that he heard the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, say, It is great treachery to tell something to your brother so that he believes you when you are lying to him."""
"394","Ibn 'Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, Do not dispute with your brother. Do not make fun of him. Do not make a promise to him and then break it."""
"395","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, There are two courses that my Community will not abandon:wailing and attacking a person's lineage."""
"396","A woman called Fusayla said that she heard her father say, I asked"","" 'Messenger of Allah"","" is it part of disobedience for a man to help his people in something which is unjust?' 'Yes"",""' he replied."""
"397","Abdullah bin Salah narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Abdullah bin Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Auf bin al-Harith bin al-Tufayl, who was the son of the brother of A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her. She was told that Abdullah bin Zubayr said in a sale or gift, ""A'isha gave it to me."" By Allah, A'isha would either be pleased or would be angry with me. She said, ""Is this what he said?"" They said, ""Yes."" She said, ""It is a vow to Allah that I will not speak to Ibn Zubayr ever again."" So Ibn Zubayr sought refuge with the Muhajireen when his hijra was prolonged. She said, ""By Allah, I will not seek refuge with anyone ever again, nor will I fulfill my vow which I vowed ever again."" When Ibn Zubayr's hijra was prolonged, he spoke to the Messenger of Allah and Abdullah bin Asad bin Yaghuth, who were both from the tribe of Zuhra. He said, ""I will avenge you with Allah unless you allow me to enter upon A'isha."" He said, ""For it is not permissible for her to vow to abstain from her family."" The Messenger of Allah and Abdullah bin Asad bin Yaghuth came to A'isha, and they said, ""Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. May we enter?"" She said, ""Enter."" They said, ""Is it for all of us, O mother of the believers?"" She said, ""Yes, enter all of you."" A'isha did not know that Ibn Zubayr was with them, so when they entered, Ibn Zubayr entered the hijab, and A'isha took refuge with him and began to weep, and the Messenger of Allah and Abdullah bin Asad bin Yaghuth began to weep with her, except that they would say, ""You have known that the Messenger of Allah has forbidden what you have known about the hijra, and that it is not permissible for a man to leave his brother for more than three nights."" They continued to remind and release until Ibn Zubayr spoke, and then A'isha began to remember and weep, saying, ""I have vowed, and the vow is severe."" They did not leave her until Ibn Zubayr spoke, and then she freed forty slaves, and after that, she would remember and weep until her tears would wet her hair."","" and I will not ever break my vow that I have vowed."" When it went on long for Ibn Az-Zubair"","" he spoke to Al-Miswar bin Makhramah and 'Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Aswad bin Yaghut and they were from Bani Zuhrah. So he said to them: ""I beseech you in the Name of Allah that you enter me upon (the place of) 'Aishah because it is unlawful for her to vow to sever relations with me."" So Al-Miswar and 'Abdur-Rahman approached with him under their upper garments until they sought her permission"","" saying: ""As-salamu 'alaiki wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu! Shall we come in?"" 'Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Come in"","" They asked: ""All of us"","" o mother of the believers?"" She said: ""Yes all of you"","" and she did know that Ibn Az-Zubair was with them. So"","" when they entered"","" Ibn Az-Zubair entered the screened place and hugged 'Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) and began beseeching her and wept. And Al-Miswar and 'Abdur-Rahman began to plead her to but speak to him and to accept from him"","" also saying to her: ""You know that the Messenger Allah ﷺ forbade what you know of abandonment and that it is not permissible for a man to abandon his brother over three nights."" He said: So when they did a great deal of reminding and urging"","" she began remind them and weep"","" saying: ""I have made a vow which is a matter of very serious nature."" They persisted in their appeal till she spoke with 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair. Then she freed forty slaves as an expiation for breaking her vow. Later on she would remember"","" after freeing forty slaves"","" then she would weep so much that her veil would become wet with tears."""
"398","Anas ibn Malik reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, Do not hate one another nor envy one another nor shun one another. Slaves of Allah"","" be brothers! It is not lawful for a Muslim to refuse to speak to his brother (Muslim) for more than three nights."""
